cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  twininvalidate: a model-invalidation monitor for a linear-Gaussian digital
  twin, with detection delay reported against false-alarm rate per change type
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A model-invalidation monitor for a declared linear-Gaussian digital twin.
  The residual generator is a fixed-gain steady-state Kalman filter whose
  innovation is normalised to a dimensionless sequence that is i.i.d. standard
  normal in control, a property measured rather than assumed. Three asset-side
  changes are injected by committed seeded scripts: an actuator-gain step, the
  same gain ramped, and a process-noise variance change. Three analytic
  sequential detectors are implemented first -- a two-sided tabular CUSUM, an
  EWMA, and a windowed generalised-likelihood-ratio test for an unknown-onset
  mean shift -- and every threshold is set from a declared in-control
  average-run-length target using in-control data only, by exact closed form
  where one exists and otherwise by bisection on a right-censored
  maximum-likelihood estimator. The deliverable is the detection-delay against
  false-alarm-rate curve per change type. Measured results that went against
  expectation are published rather than removed: the CUSUM is faster than the
  windowed GLR on all three change types; the noise-variance change takes
  three to four times longer than a comparable parameter step for every
  method, because it leaves the residual mean at zero; a correctly specified
  variance CUSUM given the post-change residual variance in advance is the
  slowest method on that change, not the fastest; and an isotonic-calibrated
  random-forest drift classifier on windowed residual features, benchmarked at
  the same declared false-alarm budget, loses to the CUSUM on two of three
  in-distribution scenarios and three of four out-of-distribution ones,
  detecting two per cent of runs on a change of the same magnitude and the
  opposite sign where every analytic baseline detects all of them. The package
  also demonstrates, by a paired simulation whose two residual streams differ
  by 6.17e-14, that twin invalidation and asset fault cannot be distinguished
  from the residual alone. Validation level 3, research grade. Not
  flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - digital-twin
  - model-invalidation
  - change-detection
  - cusum
  - ewma
  - generalised-likelihood-ratio
  - average-run-length
  - kalman-filter-residual
  - aerospace-assurance
